# Generated audit and experiment logs. Untracked deliberately, not deleted:
# `audits/` was produced by an automated review pass and contains conclusions
# that later measurement contradicted, and `experiments/` holds 65 per-iteration
# reports from a tuning loop. Both are working notes, and a public repository
# is the wrong place to publish either as if they were findings.
audits/
experiments/

# No loose Markdown at the repository root. Documentation belongs in `docs/`
# or beside what it documents; a file dropped at the root is almost always a
# working note, and this repository accumulated several. README.md is the one
# exception because GitHub reads it from exactly here.
#
# `AGENTS.md` is excluded by this rule and that is deliberate: 7,312 lines of
# internal operating instructions for AI agents is not project documentation,
# and it stays on disk where the tooling reads it.
/*.md
!/README.md
